From: LightCraft additional extensions <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:34:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Before/After shows before against after
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Before view never borrows the edited stand-ins: until the Before
render arrives (or when it fails), an edited photo's Before side is a
neutral frame saying "Rendering before…" or why it failed, in Show
Original, side by side, top/bottom and both wipes; the preview and the
thumbnail still stand in when the photo's settings are its before
settings (#2248, adapted from upstream PR #3993). A failed Before render
under a stand-in raises the failure pill as the After's does.

Y, Shift+Y, Alt+Y and Alt+Shift+Y outside the Detail view (a grid,
Compare, Survey, Reference, the Print module) open the photo in the
Detail view with that layout, as Lightroom Classic's Y goes from Library
to Develop's Before/After; in Compare it opens the select. The bottom
bar's Before/After button and the View menu's checks light up only where
the layout is on screen.

Wipes label their Before and After sides as side by side does; Show
Original's Before pill is larger with an accent outline; the edit guide
says \ toggles the original instead of "hold".

Copy Before's Settings to After and Swap keep the current crop and
orientation, which the Before view shows, instead of the raw before
settings' frame.

zh-Hans / zh-Hant: 正在渲染修改前… / 正在算繪編輯前…, and the failure line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
